A||||27||fiero56||Wierdest thing...||||1||
Z||000000||fiero56||11-05-2000||11:33 PM||||Yesterday, Saturday night, I head upstairs to go to bed. Its about 12:30-12:40am when I finally make it to bed. I fall asleep soon after. I half wake up, that feeling where you are still asleep, but somewhat concious. Well, I feel this heavy pressure, like the back of a pen, pushing against my stomach, not terribly heavy, but enough to be quite uncomfortable. I feel this for what must have been a minute or two. I then snap awake, and I feel like I have just awakened from a deep sleep, like as if I slept for 12 hours straight, and woke up in the deepest mode of sleep. I turn to look at the clock, to see what time it is, and it is 1:20am, I have only been asleep for 40 minutes. Then, almost instantly, the light above my bed turns on, by itself, illuminating my room. I am quite groggy, but there is no way I could have been able to reach it to turn it on. My door is still closed, and nothing is in my room that could have turned it on. This scares the $hit out of me, since the light is no-where near the door to reach from the door, and I get out of bed. The door to my room was closed tight, as I left it when I went to bed, and it is still closed. No-one is awake, and I head back to bed, trying to convince myself, it is all in my head, evne though I have to turn off the light that mysteriously turned on. I even check my stomach for anything. The wierd part is even today, several times, that wierd pressure has come back. I can't describe exactly how it feels, I don't know the words for it, but this is wierd.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cheever2||11-05-2000||11:41 PM||||Well, after all, you ARE in the area with the most haunted houses per capita in the world.  Most likely swamp gas though.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||11-05-2000||11:48 PM||||I've lived in this house for 8 years, and from what I re-call, we are the third owners. 8 years and trouble free, but over the last several weeks, I have been noticing some weird things, I see "blurs" out of the corner of my eye, but when I turn to look, the "blur" is gone. A blur, as I call it, is part of a room that is still colored and all, but is blurry, kind of like a heat wave. Really wierd, and I have been seeing several a week lately.<P>I had no idea Ohio had many "hauntings". Highest per capita? Thats wierd too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever2||11-06-2000||12:05 AM||||And you have lived in SW Ohio how long?!  Specifically, Waynesville has the most for one village (I lived there 4 years).<BR>I'm keeping my opinions out of this, by the way, both spiritual and speculative.  Enough people excel at that.  Certainly won't try to tell you it's nothing though, I'll believe whatever you say you experienced.  But there's plenty of books in your local library about haunted houses in those parts.  I SHOULD be guiding you to other resources however, like Clearcreek Chapel in Springboro.  Check it out, great people.<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||11-06-2000||12:17 AM||||The thing is I don't believe in ghosts, hauntings, or any of that stuff, goes against my faith. <BR>But, here I am drinking Mt. Dew, and listening to The Offspring because I don't want the same thing happening again tonight. I'm sure I will sleep sometime. I would easily dismiss everything, but when that light suddenly flicked on, I noticed. <BR>Waynesville isn't too far away, and Springboro is about 10 minutes down the road from me. I attend RELC, a WELS church, and am pretty strong in my faith, but even the strongest can have moments of wonderment.<P>I wouldn't mind hearing any of your opinions. <p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 11-06-2000).]||||reg||1
