Z||000009||Shiner||11-06-2000||03:15 AM||||Okay, I'm not afraid to say it.  That sounds very much like a "ghost" to me.  Everybody things they are something different, so the general idea of a ghost may not be against your religion.  I realize that weird things do happen, and happen all the time.  But there is a difference between weird and something you just know was'nt a coincidence.  The easiest way to tell is that feeling you have when something happens and when you think about it.  Those hairs in the back of your neck stand at attention, you get goosebumps and the chills.  You just KNOW.  You be the judge.  <P> I live in an old town on the Deleware in PA which is fairly haunted.  Pretty much all of the houses on my extended block are currently haunted or were at one point.  This house dates back to 1894, and we had some weird things happen back when we moved in.  The local firehouse is haunted by a ghost named Howie.  The fire fighters will NOT go into the engine room or the bathroom alone after 10pm, because Howie, a firefighter who died on the job, shows up.  Just about everyone who lives here has a ghost story to tell.  <P> But the pain in the abdomen sounds like a coincidence.  Get your doctor to check it out sometime if you are worried.  ||||reg||1
Z||000010||87ECO5||11-06-2000||07:25 AM||||We had something strange happen at our house about two years ago.  One evening while sitting in the living room watching TV, I turned to see my golden retriever "watch" something walk up the stairs.  I couldn't see anything but, whatever it was, she followed it - one step at a time - until it reached the top of the steps.  I decided to investigate when she went up the steps.  When I got to the top of the steps, she was standing in the hallway, scratching at the wall underneath the doorway to the attic.<P>I later found out the wife of the house's previous owner died in the house from an illness.<P>I'm with Shiner on the abdomen thing.  Call your doctor!||||reg||1
Z||000011||fiero56||11-06-2000||08:21 AM||||Well, nothing that I am sure happened, happened, and I need to have proof to convince myself, like having to physically turn off that light.<P>I went to bed, don't remember what time. I always fall asleep with the radio on, I need a constant sound, otherwise the smallest noises wake me up, so the radio drowns everything out. There were several(2) times, just as I was falling asleep(half awake)that I heard the sound of my closet door sliding on its tracks. It was enough to snap me back awake, every time, I turned on a light, the door was still where I left it. Then, just after I had fallen asleep, there was this light, kind of like when you can see a bright light even though your eyes are closed, that kept getting brighter. Then there was a crash somewhere in my room, the light disappeared, and I snapped awake. Nothing but darkness. <P>I decieded I needed to turn the radio up louder than I have ever fallen asleep with it at before. That did the trick, I heard nothing the rest of the night.<P>Got your e-mail Steve. I'll reply later this morning, when at school.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Black88GT||11-06-2000||11:20 AM||||&lt;x-files music playing&gt;<P> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/net2/alien.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000013||overlord||11-06-2000||02:08 PM||||creepy stuff....good thing its the middle of the day right now.<P>reminds me of one of my aunt's across the coutry. She purchased a house "said to be haunted", and right away noticed strange things, bumps in the night...So after many weird things she consluted the previous owners about it, they said same things happend while they were there...Now, i dont really beleive in ghosts but what changed my mind is this picture she took of the outside of the house.<BR>In one of the windows you can clearly see a  woman with kind of a "blurry hazniness" around her, just looking out the window.<P>I am going to try and find that picture and see if i can get it scanned.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Cliff Pennock||11-06-2000||02:16 PM||||I don't have an opinion about wether or not "ghosts" exist. I can however offer you a more down to earth explanation: perhaps you are sleep-walking. My fiancee is a sleepwalker also. She will get up in the middle of the night, walk to the other room, turn on the lights and go back to bed. I can even talk to her when she sleepwalks and she usually responds with some gibberish. Sometimes when she gets back to bed she immediately wakes up and wonder who has turned on the light (she says the light woke her).<P>You also have to realise that for about 20 seconds or so after you wake up, your brain has tremendous difficulty in placing everything in the proper chronicle order. A good example for instance is that a lot of people are convinced they wake up seconds <B>before</B> the alarm-clock goes off - they are convinced they wake up, look at the alarm-clock and then it goes off while in reality it's the other way around.<P>So it might be you walked in your sleep, turned on the light, went back to bed and then woke up convinced you just saw the light turn on by itself. Like I said, I've seen my fiancee do that a zillion times.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>People usually sleepwalk when there's something wrong physically (maybe the pain in your abdomen?). Your brain will not go into complete rest-state since it needs to direct a lot of energy to the problem area. This can also result in random firing of some parts of the brain - most notably the parts that handles your senses (you'll see light flashes or hear things, etc.).<P>So my diagnosis: you could be sleep-walking...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||RiceCooker||11-06-2000||02:25 PM||||I totally believe in ghosts because I know people who have had them and there are way too many documented for them to be fake. Just talking about it, like now, gives me the heebie- jeebies.<BR>I know that when someone is possessed their body is taken over by a demon and they kind of go to their stomach. Like in the Exorcist. I remember as a kid growing up, we never saw any horror movies so the first time i saw one was in seventh grade at my friend Justin's birthday party. Well, it was the exorcist and I swear to you all I was scared for years. I had to sleep with a nightlight, etc. To this day, if I think about it i still get scared. <BR>The movie just came back out and for some reason I want to go see it again. Maybe it's just to try and conquer my fears or something.<BR>Anyways, I hope your stomach is okay.<P>P.S. Is the fiero scared too?||||reg||1
