Z||000020||DaRkLoRD||11-06-2000||07:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87ECO5:<BR><B> Same goes for extra terrestrials.  Does that mean they're real too?     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I certainly believe they're real.. definitely not trying to flame anyone here, but to think humans are alone in the universe is simply ludicrous..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000021||Cooter||11-06-2000||07:36 PM||||I will add this story to the paranormal (sp?) discussion here.<BR>A co-worker's sister bought an old antique dresser with the mirror. It is the kind that has the two arms on the side of the mirror to hold it in place. They used it in an extra bedroom, so it was not seen everyday. One day, they go in and the mirror is turned against the wall. The husband and brother have to slide the dresser away from the wall and flip the mirror back around. The next day, it is flipped again. Then weird stuff started happening- noises etc. The kids in the house say they have seen "the lady that lives in the mirror" before- but what they saw was not a complete person, just the upper body. You know- what you would see standing in front of the mirror! Kinda spooky.||||reg||1
